---
// Architecture component - How TIS RMS works on campus
---

<section id="architecture" class="relative bg-[#09110c] py-24 border-t border-white/5 text-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#4ade80] uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">How It's Set Up</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
        Works on your school's network — no internet needed.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        TIS RMS runs on a designated school computer. Teachers connect through the school Wi-Fi or cable network. Everything stays inside the school.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 cards -->
    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/8 bg-white/3 p-7 text-center">
        <div class="text-4xl mb-4">🖥️</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">Teacher Computers</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Teachers use the Windows desktop app on their workstations or the Android app on their phones to scan documents.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#16a34a]/30 bg-[#16a34a]/5 p-7 text-center">
        <div class="text-4xl mb-4">🏫</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">School Server PC</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          One designated school computer acts as the server. It stores all records and runs quietly in the background — always on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/8 bg-white/3 p-7 text-center">
        <div class="text-4xl mb-4">📡</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">School Wi-Fi / LAN</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          All devices communicate through the local school network. No data leaves the campus — private and fast.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- 3 benefit cards -->
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/8 bg-white/3 p-6">
        <h4 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Works Without Internet</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Teachers can access and update records even when the school's internet connection is slow or down.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/8 bg-white/3 p-6">
        <h4 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Student Data Stays Private</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          All student records are stored only on school hardware — never uploaded to any external service or cloud.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/8 bg-white/3 p-6">
        <h4 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Fast Local Performance</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Because everything runs on your local network, searching and loading records is instant across all workstations.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
